@reactions favour
// Writer-commons, reactions batch 2. A favour done (social's cue favour, one day); .you when you did it.

? !cue:favour.you
- Someone did someone a good turn yesterday. Word gets round on a ship this size.
- Did you hear? Someone helped someone out. Nice to hear, that.
? cue:favour.you tier>=acquaintance
- I heard you helped someone out. That's the Wren way.   #warm
- I hear you did someone a favour. Good. It comes back round.
- You did a favour for someone yesterday? People notice. In a good way.
? cue:favour.you tier>=friend
- I heard what you did. Typical you. Don't let them take advantage, mind.   #warm
? cue:favour.you dept:galley
- Heard you've been helping people. Come and get a biscuit. That's how it works here.   #warm
? cue:favour.you dept:store
- Heard you've been doing favours. I've seen your ledger. You've earned a cheap tea.   #funny
